What:		/dev/binder_stats
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		OnePlus MIDAS Binder transaction accounting device. The Android 14
		9R ioctl protocol exposes version 1, per-client filters, bounded
		double-buffered records, and an mmap view of caller, destination,
		service-name, and transaction-count fields.

		Android 14 servicemanager additionally uses control 120 to register
		its process and control 121 with an `int handle` plus a bounded
		32-byte service name. Both controls return zero on success.

		Opening the device registers the Binder transaction notifier, but
		collection remains disabled until userspace issues control 101 with
		value 1. Closing the final client unregisters the notifier. This keeps
		the production-enabled kernel interface dormant when MIDAS is idle.

Users:		OnePlus Android 14 PowerStats and MIDAS services
